; RockCluster5 — 5th of 6 Rock terrain cluster variants (content-variety pass Task 6,
; 2026-08-26), the first MOSSY variant added since the original 2026-08-16 look-pass
; (RockCluster1..4). Composes 2x Rock_Moss_2.fbx + 1x Rock_Moss_5.fbx (Ultimate Nature
; Pack by Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal — License.txt at
; `source-content/assets/Ultimate Nature Pack - Jun 2019.../License.txt` re-checked before import,
; per asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate). Recorded in
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_ultimate_nature_pack.tres (extends that pack's
; existing assets_used list — same pack already supplies Rock_1/Rock_Moss_3, same reuse
; posture Task 5 used for BirchTree_1/BushBerries_1).
;
; NOT quaternius_poly_pizza_nature.tres: that file's assets_used are individually-
; downloaded poly.pizza pages (Rock_2.glb, RockMediumMoss.glb, RocksCluster.glb — used by
; RockCluster2/3/4). Rock_Moss_2 and Rock_Moss_5 are instead 2 of the 7 Rock_Moss_N.fbx
; files that ship inside the Ultimate Nature Pack extraction directory itself (confirmed
; on disk: Rock_Moss_1..7.fbx all present under that pack's FBX/ folder) — the SAME pack
; RockCluster1's Rock_Moss_3 piece and the Den prop already draw from, so this is a
; same-pack reuse case, attributed accordingly. Rock_Moss_3 deliberately NOT reused here
; (already used by RockCluster1 and the Den prop) — Rock_Moss_2 and Rock_Moss_5 chosen so
; this pass adds genuinely new pieces, not a third use of the same file.
;
; SCALE (measured via a one-off SceneTree AABB script, same procedure as Task 5's
; BirchTree/DeadTree/etc, not guessed): Rock_Moss_2.fbx raw global AABB height 0.691754
; (footprint 0.612546 x 0.650426); Rock_Moss_5.fbx raw global AABB height 0.576739
; (footprint 0.663190 x 0.914783). Both pieces used TWICE below at different per-instance
; scales to vary silhouette within the cluster (same technique RockCluster1 mixes Rock_1
; at two different scales):
;   - Rock_A (Moss_2): scale 0.318053 -> height 0.220.
;   - Rock_B (Moss_2): scale 0.231311 -> height 0.160.
;   - Rock_C (Moss_5): scale 0.346790 -> height 0.200.
; Max piece height 0.220, matching the existing 4 clusters' ~0.25 height cap (D-42,
; rock.tres's own header) — the SAME cap, not a new number. FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF: the
; exact per-piece scale/spacing is a first-pass judgment call, same open question every
; prior cluster variant carries.
;
; Slab uses the same mossier grey-green tint as RockCluster3.tscn (Color(0.48, 0.52,
; 0.42, 1)), 1.0x0.2x1.0 (post the "SLAB WIDENED 0.94 -> 1.0" cross-tile seam fix every
; current-generation terrain slab already carries).
;
; EVERYTHING NESTED UNDER ONE NODE NAMED "Slab" (a direct MeshInstance3D, matching
; RockCluster3/4's convention exactly, not BirchTree/PineTree's wrapper-Node3D
; convention) — required, not cosmetic: OcclusionFader (scripts/world/occlusion_fader.gd)
; only skips a node by that exact name.
